    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d716">

                <pb facs="0757" n="745" xml:id="pg745"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.8830 Brazil/87: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-10-14T19:00:00-04:00">October 14, 1942—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3083. Your 4108, October 10, 5 p.m. Please cable urgently monthly distribution by
                    consignees of 3,500 tons of newsprint for November and December and 3,000 tons
                    thereafter. The Department will support shipments of these amounts in accordance
                    with Embassy’s recommendation.</p>
                <p>Since August 20, 10,539 tons have been approved by the Board of Economic Warfare
                    and 5,057 tons were actually shipped in September in accordance with information
                    supplied to the Department by the War Shipping Administration.</p>
                <p>Circulation figures and extent of stock reductions would be appreciated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
